sttSettings.decoder_agent_prompt:
The audio decoder (ffmpeg) that {{productName}} needs in order to transcribe voice recordings could not be installed. Please get it working on this host.

What failed: {{code}} — {{detail}}
Host: {{os}} {{arch}}

{{productName}} only executes an ffmpeg whose bytes match a pinned SHA-256 digest, and it looks in exactly these places: /usr/local/bin, /opt/homebrew/bin, this operating system's own program directories, and its own digest-verified decoder store at <data home>/models/ffmpeg/. The path is never the trust anchor, so ~/.local/bin is deliberately NOT trusted and a copy left there is ignored.

Work out what this host actually needs — a package manager, a build from source, or another attempt at the decoder download — and decide for yourself whether elevated privileges are appropriate before using any. When you are done, re-check GET /api/stt/status and confirm that the Voice settings page no longer reports a missing decoder.
